 "response": "Gitrel's budget is now **$2805K**. This total depends on hand arithmetic across about 1,600 records, so the method matters as much as the number.\n\n**Approach**\n1. **Which records count.** Only Finance Office budget lines are used: the set, increase and decrease entries. Messages from Marketing, Sales, Legal, PMO, Vendor, Facilities, Operations and Engineering are ignored. Finance Office notes that don't change the amount are also ignored, such as reminders, cost center codes and audit notes.\n2. **Withdrawal chains.** Each chain is read from its last link backward. A withdrawal counts unless an active withdrawal cancels it, so a cancelled withdrawal brings its target back. Three examples:\n   - **#0002 stays withdrawn.** #0537 cancels #0092. That restores #0071, which cancels #0033. So #0005 stands, and #0002 is withdrawn.\n   - **#0008 is restored.** #1348 cancels #0194. That restores #0170, which cancels #0009. So the +$288K counts.\n   - **#0036 stays withdrawn.** #0561 cancels #0195. That restores #0099, which cancels #0040. So #0039 stands, and #0036 is withdrawn.\n3. **Running total.** Starting from the $2220K set in #0001, each remaining update was applied in record order.\n\nANSWER: $2805K",
